sommelier: track every clipboard transfer to the host, not just the last

When a host app pastes from a guest app, the host compositor sends a pipe,
sommelier gives the guest app a new pipe, and watches its read end to copy
the data to the host and tell crosvm to close the host's pipe at the end.

sommelier keeps only one event source for that. If a second transfer
starts before the first ends (GNOME's clipboard manager reads a new
selection right away, and apps ask for several types), the second replaces
the first's source. The first pipe is never read again, crosvm is never
told to close the host's end, and the host app waits on it forever.

Keep one event source per pipe, keyed by its read end.

